<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#field-artillery">Glossary</a> · Term · weapon</p><h1 class="enc-title">Field artillery</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as cannon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Field artillery refers to mobile cannon used on the battlefield. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gunpowder">Gunpowder</a> artillery transformed warfare from the fifteenth century, giving decisive advantages to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>, whose cannon at Panipat helped defeat the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>. Its absence or limited use disadvantaged states such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a> against better-armed invaders.</p></div>
